    <string name="legal_imprint_body">Provider: TechFlipsi / Fabian Kirchweger, Marktplatz 11/3, 4625 Offenhausen, Austria.\n\nScope: development and provision of the FlipsiBridge app — a tool for remote-controlling your own Android device via a relay server you run yourself.\n\nAuthorized representative: Fabian Kirchweger.</string>
    <string name="legal_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="legal_privacy_body">Controller: TechFlipsi / Fabian Kirchweger, Marktplatz 11/3, 4625 Offenhausen, Austria.\n\nData processed: the app only handles the data the bridge needs — server address, pairing code, connection and device status, plus the messages you write and actions you order. Chat content and history stay on the device.\n\nServer operator: FlipsiBridge connects only to the relay server you set up yourself. Whoever operates that server is responsible for processing on it; the app sends no data to any TechFlipsi server.\n\nEncryption: end-to-end encryption is built into the app (Settings → Encryption); whether it is active depends on your server and client configuration.\n\nYour rights (Art 15–21 GDPR): access, rectification, erasure, restriction, data portability and objection — in writing to the address above. You may also lodge a complaint with the Austrian Data Protection Authority.\n\nLegal basis: contract performance or your explicit consent (Art 6 (1) (b) and (a) GDPR). No profiling or automated decision-making takes place.</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_title">Terms of use</string>
    <string name="legal_terms_body">Use: FlipsiBridge is provided free of charge for private use.\n\nWarranty: the app is provided as is; statutory warranty is excluded to the extent legally permissible.\n\nLiability: TechFlipsi is liable only for intent and gross negligence and for personal injury. No liability for damage caused by improper use, third-party systems or data loss.\n\nYour duties: use the app only on devices you own or are authorized to use, and within applicable law.\n\nChanges: these terms may change; the current version lives in the app under Settings → About.</string>
